{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB09013 - MONDO_6875",
  "verbalization": "Befunolol is implicated in the pathogenesis of Ocular Hypertension through its association with Open-angle Glaucoma, a condition that is itself linked to Ocular Hypertension. The evidence suggests that Befunolol may exert a role in the development of Ocular Hypertension via its effects on the eye, particularly through its induction of Open-angle Glaucoma. This is supported by the presence of multiple pathways where Befunolol is linked to conditions that are causally associated with Ocular Hypertension. The shared indication of Open-angle Glaucoma across different drug–disease relationships indicates a potential mechanistic link, possibly involving the regulation of intraocular pressure or the disruption of aqueous humor outflow. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust, albeit indirect, relationship, which may be mediated through the influence of Befunolol on ocular physiology. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of targeting the underlying pathophysiology of Open-angle Glaucoma to potentially repurpose Befunolol for the treatment of Ocular Hypertension.",
